 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“Oh! not in vain those heros [sic] fell,<br>\nAmid those hours of fearful strife;<br>\nEach dying heart poured out a balm<br>\nTo heal the wounded nation’s life.<br>\nAnd from the soil drenched with their blood,<br>\nThe fairest flowers of peace shall bloom;<br>\nAnd history cull rich laurels there,<br>\nTo deck each martyr hero’s tomb. . . .<br>\nAnd ages yet uncrossed with life,<br>\nAs sacred urns, do hold each mound<br>\nWhere sleep the loyal, true, and brave<br>\nIn freedom’s consecrated ground.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Frances Ellen Watkins Harper, “The Massachusetts Fifty-Fourth,” October 10, 1863</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615834,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The context of the main idea expressed in the poem is best described as",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1171302,
     "content_html": "the battle victories of the Union Army during the Civil War"
    },
    {
     "id": 1171303,
     "content_html": "the contributions of the leadership of the Underground Railroad during the Civil War"
    },
    {
     "id": 1171305,
     "content_html": "the fighting units of African American soldiers during the Civil War"
    },
    {
     "id": 1171304,
     "content_html": "the Union victory in the Civil War"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615835,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What was the main idea of this poem?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1171309,
     "content_html": "The sacrifices made by African American troops as they fought for freedom would result in healing for the nation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1171306,
     "content_html": "African American troops fought more bravely, under worse conditions, than whites."
    },
    {
     "id": 1171307,
     "content_html": "Racial peace, harmony, and healing, although much to be desired, were ultimately impossible."
    },
    {
     "id": 1171308,
     "content_html": "Despite the terrible sacrifices made by African American soldiers, the nation remained ungrateful, and racial tension would continue."
    }
   ],
